{"candidateAnswer":"A couple of her scripts that dealt with emotional themes","evidence":"[D14:1 | 5:44 pm on 3 June, 2022] Joanna: Nate, after finishing my screenplay I got a rejection letter from a major company. It really bummed me out.\n[D3:1 | 9:27 am on 7 February, 2022] Joanna: Hey Nate, long time no see! The screenplay I sent in to the film festival has been on my mind all day everyday. I keep bouncing between crazy emotions like relief, excitement and worry! Fingers crossed a producer or director falls in love with it and it ends up on the big screen - that would be awesome!\n[D2:7 | 2:01 pm on 23 January, 2022] Joanna: Woohoo, Nate! I'm feeling a rollercoaster of emotions - relief, excitement, some anxiety - over finishing this project. Now I'm gonna submit it to some film festivals and (hopefully) get producers and directors to check it out. Here's hoping!\n[D24:12 | 2:01 pm on 21 October, 2022] Joanna: Well, I had a bit of a setback recently - another rejection from a production company.\n[D24:13 | 2:01 pm on 21 October, 2022] Nate: Bummer, Joanna. Is this the one you sent to a film contest? Rejections suck, but don't forget they don't define you. Keep at it and you'll find the perfect opportunity.","itemId":"urn:uuid:bff2a516-6d7c-51ba-8f4b-4c9aec2fdf4a","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:041ecea49baad227ccd45150e80c916bfb8387fedb6eca48fd6cd0a87b4fde36","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"Which of Joanna's screenplay were rejected from production companies?","referenceAnswer":"first screenplay on drama and romance, third screenplay on loss identity and connection","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"041ecea49baad227ccd45150e80c916bfb8387fedb6eca48fd6cd0a87b4fde36"}}]}